# E2E mode config for @axispoint/qr, TEMPLATE (tracked in git).
#
# Copy this file to .env.e2e.local (which is gitignored and machine-local) and replace the
# placeholder with the real V2 Web App /exec URL. Each dev machine (Mac or Windows) needs
# its own .env.e2e.local; the real value is never committed.
#
# `pnpm dev:e2e:qr` reads the endpoint ONLY from .env.e2e.local. If it is missing, the dev
# server fails loudly instead of silently falling back to simulated success.
#
# THE NAME CHANGED IN CODE PASS 10B. This app used to read VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT, which names
# the V1 deployment. The Contact Exchange submits a V2 contact_exchange envelope to the
# unified V2 endpoint, so it now reads the V2 name below, exactly like apps/web. If an
# existing .env.e2e.local still holds only the V1 name, `pnpm dev:e2e:qr` fails and says so;
# add the V2 entry rather than renaming the V1 one, which other tooling may still use.
#
# WARNING: e2e mode hits a REAL backend. A submission may create live records and send real
# email. It does NOT create a Calendar event: booking is a separate command.
VITE_V2_SUBMISSION_ENDPOINT=your_v2_apps_script_exec_url_here
